<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>The economic issues and policy in France - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:38:46 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>France</category><title>French environment minister quits as farm law opens door to contested pesticides</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-french-environment-minister-barbut-quits-as-farm-law-opens-door-to-contested-pesticides</link><description>
Environment Minister ⁠Monique Barbut has stepped ​down in protest after French lawmakers approved ​controversial legislation allowing the temporary reintroduction of two pesticides accused of harming bees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ff5d790a-859c-11f1-9a2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25287414896340.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ff5d790a-859c-11f1-9a2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25287414896340.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb2aac20-859d-11f1-8f3d-97e9dac3ef9e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:04:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ff5d790a-859c-11f1-9a2b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25287414896340.jpg">AP - Michel Euler</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France approves social media ban for children under 15, in EU first</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-france-approves-social-media-ban-for-children-under-15-in-eu-first</link><description>
French lawmakers have approved a ban on social media access for children under the age of 15, as concerns grow around the world over the impact social media have on the health and safety of minors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2e00d2e-2da7-11f1-94e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87LW4T8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2e00d2e-2da7-11f1-94e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87LW4T8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdd09254-8590-11f1-851f-bb981e703a77</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 05:56:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b2e00d2e-2da7-11f1-94e9-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-87LW4T8.jpg">AFP - SAEED KHAN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France’s emergency agriculture bill passed, amid divisions over pesticides</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260721-france-s-emergency-agriculture-bill-passed-amid-divisions-over-pesticides</link><description>
France’s National Assembly has approved an emergency agriculture bill after a tense overnight debate, clearing the way for the possible temporary return of two pesticides banned in the country but still authorised elsewhere in the European Union.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e944cd6-84df-11f1-80b0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2NT88R.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e944cd6-84df-11f1-80b0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2NT88R.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c3cfa30-84d9-11f1-b6db-db2ffabab7f1</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:07:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e944cd6-84df-11f1-80b0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2NT88R.jpg">© AFP - DIMITAR DILKOFF </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French MPs aim to reach agreement on social media ban in time for new school year</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260721-france-looks-to-close-deal-on-landmark-social-media-ban-for-children</link><description>
French lawmakers are mobilising to reach a compromise on legislation that would ban children under 15 from using social media, aiming to have the restrictions in place for the start of the new school year in September.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e98c450-843f-11f1-9c3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9J29KG.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e98c450-843f-11f1-9c3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9J29KG.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a5a8c74-843c-11f1-b209-37d1e99982f8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 08:40:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1e98c450-843f-11f1-9c3a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9J29KG.jpg">AFP - NICOLAS TUCAT</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's Fontainebleau forest faces long recovery after wildfires</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260720-france-s-fontainebleau-forest-faces-long-road-to-recover-after-wildfires</link><description>
The wildfires that ravaged more than 2,000 hectares of the Fontainebleau Forest have destroyed habitats and have put its diversity of plant and animal life under threat.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bb247fdc-83c0-11f1-9803-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2CE4J7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bb247fdc-83c0-11f1-9803-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2CE4J7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8aa9afda-841a-11f1-9c6d-5d87d60156c9</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 21:31:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bb247fdc-83c0-11f1-9803-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2CE4J7.jpg">AFP - LOU BENOIST</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France’s controversial Ripost public disorder law faces final test</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260720-france-s-controversial-ripost-public-disorder-law-faces-final-test</link><description>
France’s controversial “Ripost” law, aimed at strengthening the state’s response to urban unrest and public disorder, is set to face a decisive test on Monday when a joint parliamentary committee will study versions adopted by the National Assembly and the Senate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/04e4d484-2456-11f1-ac72-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-364H2R7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/04e4d484-2456-11f1-ac72-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-364H2R7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ff96cc4-81ca-11f1-831a-15234347de71</guid><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 05:12:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/04e4d484-2456-11f1-ac72-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-364H2R7.jpg">AFP - PHILIPPE LOPEZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Gym culture on the rise in France, as young people reshape ideas about exercise</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260719-gym-culture-on-the-rise-in-france-as-young-people-reshape-ideas-about-exercise</link><description>
France is better known for football, cycling, tennis and skiing than weightlifting. But gym culture is on the rise, especially among young people – many of whom have been inspired by social media, with France’s most popular YouTuber building his audience around bodybuilding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/000ec244-7f96-11f1-8dac-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/gym2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/000ec244-7f96-11f1-8dac-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/gym2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9f6fabe6-7f91-11f1-b632-87588271e398</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:47:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/000ec244-7f96-11f1-8dac-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/gym2.jpg">© Sarah Elzas/RFI</source><dc:creator>Sarah Elzas</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>The Grand Mosque of Paris, 'part of the French Republic' for 100 years</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260719-the-grand-mosque-of-paris-part-of-the-french-republic-for-100-years</link><description>
Inaugurated 100 years ago this week, the Grand Mosque of Paris is France's longest-serving Islamic place of worship and a landmark for Muslims and non-Muslims alike. From its origins as a tribute to Muslim soldiers who fought in the French army to its present as a centre of moderate Islam, rector Chems-Eddine Hafiz says it has an integral place in France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cbd1080-116f-11f1-a60c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3446566.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cbd1080-116f-11f1-a60c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3446566.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe89ee5a-8024-11f1-b544-a97de1dfa122</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 10:50:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5cbd1080-116f-11f1-a60c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Par3446566.jpg">© AFP - LIONEL BONAVENTURE </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French journalist warns of press freedom crackdown as court revives source hunt</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260719-french-journalist-lavrilleux-disclose-warns-of-judicial-crackdown-as-court-revives-source-hunt</link><description>
A French court has ordered the reopening of an investigation into journalist Ariane Lavrilleux over the highly sensitive "Egypt Papers" investigation, reviving a case that press freedom groups say could have major consequences for the protection of confidential sources in France.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f7ebef7a-d770-11ef-b4e2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36UD2WY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f7ebef7a-d770-11ef-b4e2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36UD2WY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">961f8e38-8119-11f1-92a1-57e3f657aba9</guid><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 08:32:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f7ebef7a-d770-11ef-b4e2-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_36UD2WY.jpg">AFP - ANNA KURTH</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French teen sentenced to 18 years for fatal stabbing of school supervisor</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260717-french-teen-sentenced-to-18-years-for-fatal-stabbing-of-school-supervisor</link><description>
A French court on Thursday sentenced a 15-year-old boy to 18 years in prison for murdering a school supervisor outside his secondary school in the east of the country, citing his lack of "empathy, remorse or regret". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4794f14-46f5-11f0-92b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-49WZ9K9.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4794f14-46f5-11f0-92b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-49WZ9K9.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d12bc994-81b7-11f1-a3d9-a767334b21d9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 09:26:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/a4794f14-46f5-11f0-92b1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-49WZ9K9.jpg">AFP - FRANCOIS NASCIMBENI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's wheat production to fall after heatwaves push early harvest</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260717-france-s-wheat-production-drops-after-scorching-weather-pushes-early-harvest</link><description>
The wheat harvest in France, Europe’s largest grain producer, is expected to fall by 4 percent compared to 2025 after an unusually early harvest carried out during successive heatwaves.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbb520a-811f-11f1-b078-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T210149Z-1390557597-RC2C4MAG5N9F-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbb520a-811f-11f1-b078-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T210149Z-1390557597-RC2C4MAG5N9F-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2e7d63f2-8120-11f1-a7de-6d02e2a4e797</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 08:28:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/1dbb520a-811f-11f1-b078-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-06-30T210149Z-1390557597-RC2C4MAG5N9F-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-AGRICULTURE.jpg">© Stephane Mahe/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron toughens stance on arson, with dozens arrested as wildfires sweep France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-macron-toughens-stance-on-arson-as-wildfires-sweep-france</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron has said there would be "zero tolerance" for arson after France was hit by wildfires that have scorched thousands of hectares, as multiple heatwaves since May have dried out forests and fields. Dozens have been arrested across the country over starting fires, including a volunteer firefighter.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbdc550e-8101-11f1-a945-6937b7331399</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:54:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Stéphane Mahe/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fears over foreign influence in France, as Musk backs Le Pen presidential bid</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-elon-musk-s-backing-of-le-pen-presidential-bid-raises-foreign-influence-concerns-in-france</link><description>
Billionaire Elon Musk has thrown his support behind far-right leader Marine Le Pen's bid for the French presidency, calling her "France's last hope", and prompting accusations of foreign interference in the 2027 election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65867bc2-80f8-11f1-aac2-05c808138351</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:35:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein/AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French man charged with rape and murder of schoolgirl Lyhanna</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-french-man-charged-with-rape-murder-of-schoolgirl-lyhanna</link><description>
The main suspect in the death of an 11-year-old girl whose body was found in the Gers region has been charged with the rape and murder of a child. The case has sparked nationwide protests and renewed scrutiny of the French justice system, after it emerged that the suspect had previously been accused of raping another child.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf726d0e-80e3-11f1-9ad7-11c429da1086</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:58:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French parliament passes assisted dying law after years of wrangling</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-france-passes-assisted-dying-law-after-years-of-wrangling</link><description>
France's National Assembly has given its definitive backing to legislation granting terminally ill adults the right to end their lives with medical assistance, bringing to a close a protracted and often fraught political battle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af51b17a-807d-11f1-90a2-95c1f2bcc31e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:10:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg">© REUTERS/Abdul Saboor</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Firefighters tackle flare-ups in Fontainebleau forest after reining in blaze</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260715-firefighters-tackle-flare-ups-in-fontainebleau-forest-after-fires-brought-under-control</link><description>
Around 800 firefighters were still at work in Fontainebleau forest on Wednesday morning, tackling flare-ups after the fires were brought under control the previous day, following 48 hours of intense firefighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f11e2794-802a-11f1-977a-e9047a96864f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 11:45:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg">AFP - FRANCK DESPREZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>European troops and planes join Bastille Day parade in show of unity for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-european-troops-and-warplanes-join-paris-military-bastille-day-parade-in-show-of-unity-for-ukraine</link><description>
Some 500 soldiers from the "Coalition of the Willing" backing Ukraine marched down Paris's Champs-Elysees on ​Tuesday in ‌the annual Bastille Day parade, in a showcase of support for Kyiv and a symbolic flexing of European military muscle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3fa6be6-7f63-11f1-b4bc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C24J99R.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3fa6be6-7f63-11f1-b4bc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C24J99R.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fc6904da-7f6b-11f1-a3c5-01014d2074c2</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 11:28:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c3fa6be6-7f63-11f1-b4bc-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C24J99R.jpg">AFP - LUDOVIC MARIN</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France marks 10 years since Bastille Day terror attack in Nice killed 86</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-france-marks-10-years-since-bastille-day-terror-attack-in-nice-killed-86</link><description>
Religious leaders have gathered in Nice for an interfaith service to pray for the victims of the Bastille Day terror attack, on the eve of the 10th anniversary of the atrocity that killed 86 people and injured more than 400. President Emmanuel Macron is due to lead the main memorial ceremony later on Tuesday, while a minute's silence will be observed before France's World Cup semi-final against Spain.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">aa8e1a84-7e98-11f1-83f4-efef7f7c984b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:12:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d161ffa6-7f5e-11f1-b351-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C23C7NQ.jpg">AFP - VALERY HACHE</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fifty-nine arrested over French wildfires, as Fontainebleau blaze continues</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-france-fifty-nine-arrested-over-wildfires-two-for-fontainebleau-forest-blaze-near-paris</link><description>
